        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add y-axis tick labels and plot-aware x-axis to cost history chart",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds dollar-scale y-axis tick labels to the cost history chart and replaces the hand-rolled full-width x-axis `HStack` with Swift Charts' built-in `chartXAxis`, so both axes align to the plot area instead of the container edge.\r\n\r\nCloses #1854.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n### Y-axis labels (previously hidden)\r\n\r\n- `AxisMarks(position: .leading, values: yAxisTickValues(maxCostUSD:))` renders currency-formatted tick labels on the left side.\r\n- **Compact formatting**: whole-dollar labels for values ≥ $1 (`$0`, `$757`, `$1,515`), cents preserved only for nonzero sub-dollar values (`$0.50`) to avoid duplicate `$0` ticks.\r\n- Empty tick set for flat/no data — the axis renders no labels.\r\n- Tick selection: `[]` for ≤ 0, `[0, max]` for < $1, `[0, mid, max]` for ≥ $1.\r\n\r\n### X-axis (plot-aware)\r\n\r\n- Replaced the manual `HStack` (which spanned the full card width and ignored the y-axis gutter) with `chartXAxis { AxisMarks(values: model.axisDates) }`.\r\n- Edge labels use explicit anchors: first date `.topLeading`, last date `.topTrailing` — prevents the right-side label from being clipped.\r\n- Removed `axisLabelAreaHeight`, `axisLabelTopPadding`, and the manual date `HStack`. Chart height bumped from 114 → 130 to accommodate the built-in axis.\r\n\r\n### Detail/tooltip costs unchanged\r\n\r\n- `yAxisCostString` is chart-local; all detail rows, tooltips, and summary totals still use `UsageFormatter.currencyString` with cents.\r\n\r\n## Screenshot\r\n\r\n<img width=\"799\" height=\"600\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04010ea0-0f8d-47d5-a5c0-4edb6b0b0930\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1528\" height=\"2446\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f6b58f8d-4ef6-4454-b63b-3a1ce68f2772\" />\r\n\r\n## Video\r\n\r\nhttps://cap.so/s/p2506ammwdttz9w\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- 4 new focused tests in `CostHistoryChartMenuViewTests`:\r\n  - Y-axis tick values: empty for ≤ 0, two ticks < $1, three ticks ≥ $1.\r\n  - Y-axis cost labels: `$0` for zero, `$13` for 12.56, `$0.50` for sub-dollar nonzero.\r\n- `swift test --filter CostHistoryChartMenuViewTests` — 13/13 pass.\r\n- `make check` — 0 SwiftFormat/SwiftLint violations.\r\n- Full `make test` — passes except one unrelated-by-area failure in `ClaudeOAuthCredentialsStoreCLIStorageOwnershipTests` (OAuth/keychain ownership, not chart code).\r\n- Live UI verification via CUA automation confirmed both axis label sets render correctly.",
